{title: Greensleeves}
{artist: Tradicionál (Anglie, 16. století)}
{key: Ami}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse}
A[Ami]las, my [G]love, you [Ami]do me [E]wrong,
to [Ami]cast me [G]off dis[Ami]cour[E]teous[Ami]ly.
For [Ami]I have [G]loved you [Ami]well and [E]long,
de[Ami]lighting [G]in your [E]compa[Ami]ny.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Greensleeves was [G]all my [Ami]joy,
and [E]Greensleeves was my de[E]light,
[C]Greensleeves was my [G]heart of [Ami]gold,
and [Ami]who but my [E]lady Green[Ami]sleeves.
{end_of_chorus}
